-- Universe expansion batch 1 (V5) added 12 new instruments with zero price history - Technical
-- and Sector scoring for them would be meaningless without it. Same real backfill approach as
-- Module 1.5's original V2 seed: fetched every weekday's file (2026-04-09 through 2026-07-28, the
-- exact same window as the original 8's backfill so the whole 20-instrument universe shares one
-- consistent history range) from NSE's real sec_bhavdata_full archive
-- (archives.nseindia.com/products/content/sec_bhavdata_full_DDMMYYYY.csv), filtered to SERIES=EQ
-- and each target symbol anchored to the start of the line - an early unanchored substring match
-- attempt wrongly matched things like "XITC, EQ," as a hit for "ITC, EQ,", caught and fixed
-- before this data was ever written, not after.
--
-- All 79 weekday URLs in the window returned HTTP 200, but only 75 distinct trading dates ever
-- landed - the same 75 as the original 8's backfill, for the same reason: NSE doesn't 404 a
-- market-holiday date, it serves a copy of the prior real trading day's file under that date's
-- URL, same DATE1 field and all. That surfaced as 4 exact-duplicate (symbol, trade_date) pairs
-- per new instrument in the raw fetch (30-Apr/27-May/25-Jun/13-Apr each appearing twice) - caught
-- by comparing the URL-date count against the values file's distinct-date count before writing
-- this migration, not discovered after the fact, and correctly collapsed by
-- ON CONFLICT (instrument_id, trade_date) DO NOTHING below. CLOSE_PRICE (the official adjusted
-- close) is used, not LAST_PRICE, matching the original backfill's column choice. sma200/
-- weekly_sma30 will remain unavailable for these 12 too, same disclosed reason as the original 8:
-- 75 days is short of the 200/~150 days those indicators need.
--
-- ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING: a live pipeline run may already have inserted today's row for some of
-- these symbols under the docker/prod profile; this migration only fills gaps.
